{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":1,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:20:37.745258193Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"694ce058-641b-4635-a7f6-91dc351c2532","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=stress-tested all 6 mandate areas + crosslink fork parser grammar from source (design_doc.rs/swarm/init.rs/budget.rs); findings drafted next=post findings comments + final verdict blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:20:37.734417550Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAw22JnwxpRIkRoYGHsb5kCE32b9jhhRRC2kB/oIFLzM7zc8FzzpkT/mV6NrNN/CYv5HEimx5nyaTXXXiaPYJLCw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHbrbPn16Ssr+yOe3jQ5lsAK7w/L2ezIvyR0T8mblrbq084IWM/r3vRxoUrpRW1MhoPicXDuNan2TQXG4WVedgc="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":2,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:20:54.530455905Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"bbf09248-6759-4b3e-9d6f-e5b913ad51d4","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"PRIMARY ADVERSARIAL REVIEW #433 (hy3, independent of muse-spark pass) — FINDINGS PART 1/3 (A,B,C). Lens: re-derive from source, distrust doc self-claims.\n\nFINDING A [MUST-FIX / launch-blocking] Replan doc structurally incompatible with crosslink fork design_doc parser.\n- statement: .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md is marked 'consumed_by: crosslink swarm init --doc' but uses ONLY H1 ('#') headings ('# Purpose', '# Phase DIS', '# Phase R0' ... '# Swarm Parameters') and has NO '## Requirements' H2. Source crosslink/src/commands/design_doc.rs: sections switch ONLY on H2 ('## ', line 94); every H1 resets title + section=Title (lines 80-91); flush_block(Title) is a no-op (line 125). So ALL body content between H1s is discarded -> requirements and requirement_groups are EMPTY. swarm/init.rs:18 calls parse_design_doc. Net: 'crosslink swarm init --doc epic-423-swarm-replan.md' parses to a DesignDoc with ZERO work units -> swarm launches nothing.\n- why-unverified: the #423 kickoff (22:03) only edited the PLAN doc and explicitly admitted it 'did NOT verify swarm-init parser behavior.' The replan (the actual consumed_by target) was never checked against the grammar.\n- cheapest discriminating test: run 'crosslink swarm init --doc .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md' in a scratch worktree and inspect parsed requirement count; or unit-test parse_design_doc(replan_text) -> assert requirement_groups.len() > 0.\n- severity-if-wrong: total swarm init failure (zero agents). MUST FIX before launch.\n\nFINDING B [HIGH] DIS acceptance instance #2 is self-healed; worktree docs still assert it as broken.\n- statement: worktree docs list 'unverifiable playbook section citations reported by issue #429 researcher' as a known-broken DIS instance. But #429 auditor (pp3g-JUF0) posted a PROVENANCE CORRECTION: those citations were phantom-at-write (2026-08-18, playbook absent) and SELF-HEALED (playbook now exists with 5.1-5.9 incl. cited numbers). MAIN repo plan doc (line 9) already corrected this ('four verified current instances' + temporal-healing clause). Worktree copies are stale.\n- why-unverified: worktree docs predate the #429 correction.\n- cheapest discriminating test: confirm agent-orchestration-playbook.md 5.3/5.4/5.6/5.8 exist (they do) -> instance #2 is not currently broken.\n- severity-if-wrong: DIS acceptance gate trains/tests on a phantom -> gate validity undermined. Medium.\n\nFINDING C [HIGH] DIS acceptance instance #4 ('stale git claim in auditor kickoff text') is not locatable; catchability unverifiable.\n- statement: design docs assert a 'stale git claim in auditor kickoff text' as a known-broken instance. I read auditor.md in full, read kickoff-custom-template.md, and grepped /home/claude-code/.crosslink and /home/claude-code/.claude for 'stale git'/'git claim' -> the phrase appears ONLY in the design docs themselves, never at the asserted source. The main repo plan doc still lists it as 'verified current' but I cannot verify that verification.\n- why-unverified: instance source not accessible/identifiable from reviewer scope; may live in built-in KICKOFF.md inside the crosslink binary (not inspectable) or operator private notes.\n- cheapest discriminating test: locate the exact 'stale git claim' string in auditor kickoff text (grep -r 'stale git' ~/.crosslink/rules/kickoff.md and built-in template) and confirm it is both stale and present. Until located, DIS cannot be validated against this instance.\n- severity-if-wrong: if the claim is a phantom (like #2), the DIS 'must catch all four' criterion is unsatisfiable for that instance. Medium-High.","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:20:54.524125622Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAQ/xrc+Hir1xpluvhqKcrvDF7hEEVrdNRdY8slu52l2VOJF8Gca4k4YZtRgIRlvV3+opGJtcqEDVW8dqDDu+jBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGUWW07xhVX01uOB+JX0VM8S9+wI40tjh/CmCUsaYAXry+vQb65JK9lo9onKSmdrXO0vqi4gBnf0ADAMZWLitgE="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":3,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:21:10.176232131Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"92fb58f5-8812-4c6a-8507-1aee507948ff","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"PRIMARY ADVERSARIAL REVIEW #433 (hy3) — FINDINGS PART 2/3 (D,E,F).\n\nFINDING D [HIGH] Budget-window 'hard limit / agents terminated' (playbook 5.2) is unimplemented in visible source; replan calls it a 'guide' (contradiction).\n- statement: playbook 5.2 (lines 189-190): 'Budget windows are hard limits. Agents exceeding the budget are terminated.' But swarm budget.rs contains ONLY config (config_budget), estimation (estimate_phase_cost, default_agent_duration) and budget_recommendation -> NO termination/kill logic. Grep across the swarm module found only a '// Cost exceeds budget' comment (mod.rs:783). The replan says 'Budget window: 6h total guide' -> directly contradicts the playbook's 'hard limit.'\n- why-unverified: playbook asserts enforcement; source shows only recommendation. Whether termination exists in the orchestrator/sentinel path is unverified.\n- cheapest discriminating test: grep -rn 'terminate|kill' crosslink/src/commands/swarm/ (done -> none) and check whether any caller enforces budget_window_s as a hard cutoff; also inspect orchestrator/sentinel. If no enforcement code exists, the 'hard limit' is aspirational.\n- severity-if-wrong: if not a hard limit, the 6h 'guide' is de-facto behavior and the swarm could run unbounded or be mis-scoped; reliance on the playbook claim for sequencing is unsound. Medium-High.\n\nFINDING E [MEDIUM] D1-D9 delta claims are single-source, self-admitted unverified; design docs inherit them as established.\n- statement: replan/plan present D1-D9 (fork deltas) as the foundation for R2 parity probes and R3 verdict. But #427 matrix is explicitly a read-only breadth-first probe that 'did NOT run the harness', 'did NOT probe opencode2 beta', and lists 5 WHAT-NOT-TESTED items. Deltas are evidence-based for v1 fork but UNKNOWN for v2 beta. Design docs inherit them without re-derivation.\n- context: the plan's own REQ-P0A..D probes ARE the re-verification (good), but they are gated on R2 (late). Early phases (DIS, R0, R1) assume the deltas are real without independent check.\n- cheapest discriminating test: promote at least one independent fork-vs-source delta confirmation (e.g. run the 16-row hang matrix from #427) before R3 gating, not after.\n- severity-if-wrong: if any D1-D9 is mischaracterized (e.g. D2/D3 already landed upstream), the R3 verdict gate could be wrong. Medium.\n\nFINDING F [MEDIUM] Worktree design-doc copies are stale vs main repo; launch source ambiguous.\n- statement: my worktree's replan/plan docs carry the OLD four-instance list (incl. self-healed #2) and lack the parser-grammar instance. The MAIN repo plan doc (line 9) already has 'four verified current instances' + parser instance + temporal-healing. So worktree copies are behind. If the swarm is launched from this worktree, it consumes stale docs.\n- why-unverified: worktree not synced to main repo's corrections.\n- cheapest discriminating test: git diff main -- .design/ to confirm divergence; decide which copy is canonical for launch.\n- severity-if-wrong: launching from stale worktree docs propagates stale instance #2 and misses the parser instance. Medium.","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:21:10.170582250Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAi/WQ4fa7bmRCBGFEDpwrH1BEN5vyLgw9x9MfW59U4R217DcEkodtuTvbk6BA2+iNiHysLHOJajKes9R8BvSVAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMUv7eY3JdQ01N0Y8LH2XXSeP87yqfzPUNk7xS7N8nqRaImtB7gZPnunlTvDU7sxY1A1e3c3XtTSjpRAclcNIQw="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":4,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:21:26.674169868Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"bb7258c0-e631-45cd-b6c8-93e1f9e1f0ec","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"PRIMARY ADVERSARIAL REVIEW #433 (hy3) — FINDINGS PART 3/3 (G,H,I).\n\nFINDING G [MEDIUM] Track M assumptions from projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md not independently verified.\n- statement: replan Track M says 'lower-risk parallel environment + cutover' and 'Path updates handled systematically by projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md runbook.' The design treats the runbook as existing and authoritative. Per mandate I should verify it exists and its claims hold. I could not locate/verify it within reviewer scope (it is outside the worktree; likely in a different projects tree).\n- why-unverified: not read; existence/claims unconfirmed.\n- cheapest discriminating test: locate projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md, confirm it exists, and verify its cutover/parallel-environment claims are current (not themselves stale like permissions.md).\n- severity-if-wrong: if the runbook is missing or stale, Track M gating (M1 gated on R1, M4 on R0d) rests on a phantom. Medium.\n\nFINDING H [LOW/NIT] S1/S2/S3 definitions are accurate but understate open S1 risks.\n- statement: S1/S2/S3 match #423 definitions (good). But #423 seed findings flag unverified S1 risks: permission-matcher semantics unverified for S1 (#417), guard plugins use 1.x tool.execute.before hook API (v2 compat unverified), model-discipline.md timeout schema verified only against 1.18.11 (S1 may reschema provider.options.timeouts -> silent hang-protection loss). The design docs' S1-targeted probes (REQ-P1..P4) are the right response, but the docs present S1 as a clean surface without surfacing these open risks.\n- severity: Low (plan does include the probes). Note for dispatcher.\n\nFINDING I [LIMITATION, not a design defect] Installed binary vs source-tree divergence not fully verifiable from reviewer scope.\n- statement: mandate asked to check divergence between installed /home/claude-code/.cargo/bin/crosslink and source tree /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink. I verified the SOURCE tree's parser grammar (design_doc.rs) and budget module directly. But I could NOT (a) run 'crosslink swarm init --doc' / 'crosslink --version' (not in reviewer allowlist), nor (b) grep the binary's string table as text (ripgrep skips binary; no 'strings' in allowlist). So the installed binary's actual grammar/version is unverified. The source tree's git log was also blocked by the token-based permission matcher (rtk git / git -C denied; only 'git log .' with workdir would work and I could not confirm it).\n- implication: the already-verified 'H3+Requirements-section parser grammar empirically confirmed twice' should be re-confirmed against the INSTALLED binary before launch, since the binary may predate the source tree's '## Requirements' requirement (design_doc.rs line 352 warns when absent).\n- this is a reviewer-scope limitation to report, not a defect in the design docs.","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:21:26.668632746Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA91TrPbjms8JF3nxMZxXQnn938aVLWegnFUxlt4umM2rp+xJvbnbjuEVLloowz12ZtuZYdORb4eVWWymrTBFfDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMYY+vGC3g+9os6972+IIoqrUoblx1Woch1FeYfn1mY2dFE/oM5M/nHJZL0wmFSPvZ7bcBRh992Gtf4QM4xoNww="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-23T22:21:43.902652568Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"ad7c02f7-18fe-4542-9f11-f5c25fc82bb4","comment_uuid":"3edb5e8d-86c2-4fc5-ba9b-6abbbcc67599","author":"pp3g-4xe1-primary-adversarial-review-on-433-a-muse-spark-894c","content":"PRIMARY ADVERSARIAL REVIEW #433 (hy3) — FINAL VERDICT.\n\nVERDICT: HOLD (not launch-ready, not merely launch-with-holes).\n\nRationale: Finding A is launch-blocking on its own. The replan doc is the file explicitly marked 'consumed_by: crosslink swarm init --doc', yet its H1-only structure makes the crosslink fork parser (design_doc.rs + swarm/init.rs:18) discard all body content, yielding a DesignDoc with ZERO requirement groups -> the swarm would initialize with no work units. Until the consumed_by target parses to a non-empty requirement set, no launch is meaningful. The other findings (B,C,D,E,F,G) are serious but secondary to A; H/I are non-blocking.\n\nINDEPENDENT TOP-3 MUST-CLOSE (before any swarm launch):\n1. [from A] Make the consumed_by target parseable. Either (a) restructure .design/epic-423-swarm-replan.md to the parser grammar: add a '## Requirements' H2 and convert each '# Phase X' to '### Phase N' nested under it (mirroring the already-conformant plan doc), or (b) repoint 'consumed_by' to the conformant plan doc and ensure the replan's richer phase/gate content is preserved. Verify with 'crosslink swarm init --doc <file>' producing requirement_groups.len() > 0.\n2. [from B,C,F] Reconcile the DIS four-acceptance-instance list with current reality. Drop or locate-and-verify the self-healed instance #2 (playbook citations, per #429 provenance correction) and the unlocatable instance #4 ('stale git claim in auditor kickoff text' — not found in auditor.md, kickoff template, or .crosslink/.claude trees). Align the worktree copies with the main repo's already-corrected list ('four verified current instances' + parser-grammar instance + temporal-healing). All four acceptance instances must be real, current, and mechanically catchable before the DIS gate is trusted.\n3. [from D] Verify the budget-window hard-limit semantics. The playbook (5.2) claims 'agents exceeding the budget are terminated', but the swarm budget module implements only config/estimate/recommendation (no termination logic found). Resolve the '6h total guide' (replan) vs 'hard limit' (playbook) contradiction: confirm whether enforcement exists anywhere (orchestrator/sentinel) or the claim is aspirational, and correct the design doc accordingly before using it to bound phases.\n\nSECONDARY (should close, non-blocking): E (independently confirm >=1 fork delta before R3 gate, not after), G (verify projects/server/migration-handoff-summary.md exists/current before Track M relies on it), H (surface open S1 risks in the docs). I (installed-binary-vs-source divergence) is a reviewer-scope limitation: re-confirm the parser grammar against the INSTALLED crosslink binary before launch.\n\nNote: my worktree copies are stale vs the main repo's corrected plan doc; the operator should decide the canonical launch source. I did not read the muse-spark reviewer's findings (per isolation mandate) — divergence between our verdicts is intended signal.","created_at":"2026-08-23T22:21:43.896808975Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAzQhZOSxjwBECIC9lKGJilg+NBsv5Iv5j0hIzsItHHNVhCBwc87M3ATU9wQ7meiJWgK0Zy8gDnCvEbCUsG3P4Aw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:tUf+Yfn7YETig7tytiUbSS0xDWW/g8Ba6qDZqZ7e0pI","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg4QBetGVQo8I0gobtcd9EupgLHt0iVydD9bC43hQFVSQAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAYU2fU+L8hebw+aCUoh3jU1lCPfBnEf5McDappW56BKa